{
 "description": "Reference taxonomy (B.1.1 as amended; backlog #16 - run 2's Blocker P9b-1). CLOSURE-REQUIRED references must land in-bundle: Set members[].ref, Tailoring selects/excludes/operation targets (+ statement-id existence), Implementation component-ref/requirement-ref (+ basis-ref against the component's authorizations, D5), Finding assessment-ref/requirement-ref, Mapping source/target-scope statement ids WHEN the endpoint is in-bundle. LANDMARK references resolve outside the bundle by design: Mapping endpoints, party/authority URIs, evidence refs, external schema/reference URLs, attestation subjects (self-verifying via digest). Each vector is a mini-bundle; expected-errors 0 = closes. Decided on 2026-11-14 (backlog #83, D10): a `statement-id` anywhere inside a facet payload of a Requirement is held as a `by-statement` key is held. Alone it names a statement of the host; beside a `requirement-ref` it names a statement of that Requirement, which binds where the bundle holds it; a `requirement-ref` alone names a Requirement as a whole. A `private:` facet is not read. Fragment references (backlog #82, FRAGMENT-1; D9): `fragment-references` - each case is a mini-bundle, with the part of a manifest it needs under `manifest` where it needs one. An object refers to something as `#id` in two forms: `(#id)` in a string at any depth, the id being at least one character and none of space, tab, CR, LF and `)`; and the whole of a string that begins with `#` and is longer than that, under a member named `href`. A `private:` facet is not read, under `facets` or under an Assessment's `method`. `expected` gives the number of such references (`total`) and how many name each kind, the first kind that fits being counted, in this order: `resource` - an entry of `resources` with that `id` in the references@1 facet of the object itself or of a Set that lists it as a member, directly or through nested Sets; `object` - an object of the bundle whose id ends, after its last `/`, in that id, A to Z compared as a to z; `statement` - `<object>_<statement id>`, split at one of its `_`, the object found as before and the statement one of its own; `parameter` - the `name` of a parameter of a statement in the bundle; `source` - the `uuid` of an entry of the manifest's `provenance.sources`. `nothing` lists [object id, id] for the rest, in the order of the object ids, then of the ids named. It is a report: nothing fails by it.",
